# Build output goes to build/, the IDE's Publish output to publish/ — both are
# disposable. Nothing generated belongs in the project root: build with
# `-o build/app.exe` (see README "Run") rather than `-o app.exe`.
build/
publish/

# runtime state ([database].sqlitePath / [metrics].path, created on first start)
data/*
# committed: the original Mir2 snapshot (read-only seed), the rule tables
# every gameplay number is loaded from, and the ledger recording where those
# numbers come from. `tools/sync_rules.py` copies the tables here from
# templates/game/legend/data (the single edit source); RULES.md is written
# here by hand.
!data/M2.DB
!data/RULES.md
!data/rules/
!data/rules/**
app.db
app.db-journal
app.db-wal
uploads/
*.log
*.err
zan_crash.log

# stray artifacts, in case something was built the wrong way anyway
*.exe
*.dll
*.obj
*.o
*.lib
*.pdb
